(EXP-38: `is even`.
 Also covers: EXP-39 `is odd`, EXP-40 `is positive`, EXP-41 `is negative`,
 EXP-42 `is zero`, EXP-43 `is empty` on a list.
 Every one of the six is run against a subject that satisfies it and a subject
 that does not, because a predicate that is always true is indistinguishable
 from a predicate that is not evaluated at all.
 `is positive` is recorded against 0 as well: 0 is not positive.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-38.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   4 even
   5 not even
   5 odd
   4 not odd
   5 positive
   -2 not positive
   0 not positive
   -2 negative
   5 not negative
   0 zero
   5 not zero
   blank empty
   roster filled
)
a number called four is 4.
a number called five is 5.
a number called owed is -2.
a number called origin is 0.
a list called roster is [1, 2, 3].
a list called blank is [].
If four is even then, Print "4 even". Otherwise, Print "4 not even".
If five is even then, Print "5 even". Otherwise, Print "5 not even".
If five is odd then, Print "5 odd". Otherwise, Print "5 not odd".
If four is odd then, Print "4 odd". Otherwise, Print "4 not odd".
If five is positive then, Print "5 positive". Otherwise, Print "5 not positive".
If owed is positive then, Print "-2 positive". Otherwise, Print "-2 not positive".
If origin is positive then, Print "0 positive". Otherwise, Print "0 not positive".
If owed is negative then, Print "-2 negative". Otherwise, Print "-2 not negative".
If five is negative then, Print "5 negative". Otherwise, Print "5 not negative".
If origin is zero then, Print "0 zero". Otherwise, Print "0 not zero".
If five is zero then, Print "5 zero". Otherwise, Print "5 not zero".
If blank is empty then, Print "blank empty". Otherwise, Print "blank filled".
If roster is empty then, Print "roster empty". Otherwise, Print "roster filled".
